# CALLPOOL — hourly provisional standings. MAINNET.
#
# Hourly to match the callout poll it depends on: the sample can only be as
# complete as the store it reads, so running more often would republish the
# same inputs with a newer timestamp — which is precisely the lie the card's
# staleness warning exists to prevent.
#
# `RandomizedDelaySec=180`, wider than the poller's 90s, so the sample lands
# *after* the hour's callouts have been captured rather than racing them.
# `After=` in the unit orders them only when systemd starts both together;
# separate timers need the offset.
#
# **`Persistent=false`, unlike every other timer here.** A missed sample is not
# a missed input — an estimate for an hour that has already passed is of no use
# to anyone, and catching up on boot would publish a stale figure with a fresh
# timestamp, which is worse than the gap. The crank and the poller are
# `Persistent=true` because their inputs decide money. This one does not.

[Unit]
Description=CALLPOOL — sample provisional standings hourly (mainnet)
Documentation=https://github.com/AlphaArtrem/call-pool

[Timer]
OnCalendar=hourly
RandomizedDelaySec=180
AccuracySec=30s
Persistent=false
Unit=callpool-sample-standings.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
